- Testing under policy updates and message reordering

## Code Example
```javascript
function redact(customer, level) {
  if (level === 'full') return { name: null, email: null, card: null };
  if (level === 'partial') {
    const maskedCard = customer.card.replace(/\d(?=\d{4})/g, '*');
    const maskedEmail = customer.email.replace(/([^@]{1,2})[^@]*(@.*)/, (m, p1, p2) => p1[0] + '**' + p2);
    return { ...customer, card: maskedCard, email: maskedEmail };
  }
  return customer;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design cross-region consistency with SLA targets and fault tolerance for multi-tenant streams.

## Key Concepts
- Total order per tenant across regions
- Vector clocks and regional sequence numbers
- Barrier commits, idempotent processing, and tombstones
- Fault injection and late-arrival handling

## Code Example
```javascript
// Vector clock merge for per-tenant streams
function mergeVC(a, b) {
  const keys = new Set([...Object.keys(a), ...Object.keys(b)]);
  const out = {};
  for (const k of keys) {
    out[k] = Math.max(a[k] || 0, b[k] || 0);
  }
  return out;
}

// Regional sequencer generates monotonically increasing sequence
class RegionalSequencer {
  constructor(region) {
    this.region = region;
    this.sequences = new Map(); // tenantId -> sequence number
  }

  next(tenantId) {
    const current = this.sequences.get(tenantId) || 0;
    const next = current + 1;
    this.sequences.set(tenantId, next);
    return { tenantId, sequence: next, region: this.region };
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests per-key stateful processing, TTL-based windowing, and idempotence across replays—core KCNA concepts—while exercising cross-event aggregation and emission semantics.

## Key Concepts
- Per-key in-memory or stateful session store with a 30-second TTL
- Idempotent emits using a deterministic sessionId (userId:start)
- Out-of-order arrivals handled via lastEventTs and session boundaries
- At-least-once delivery guaranteed by committing offsets only after emit

## Code Example
```javascript
function onMessage(ctx, msg) {
  const session = sessionStore().getOrCreate(msg.userId, () => ({
    startTs: msg.timestamp,
    endTs: msg.timestamp,
    count: 0,
    lastEventTs: msg.timestamp
  }));
  session.endTs = msg.timestamp;
  session.lastEventTs = msg.timestamp;
  session.count++;
  sessionStore().setTtl(msg.userId, 30000, () => {
    ctx.emit('sessions', {
      userId: msg.userId,
      sessionStart: session.startTs,
      sessionEnd: session.endTs,
      eventCount: session.count
    });
    sessionStore().remove(msg.userId);
  });
}

function commitOffsets() {
  ctx.commit();
}

function sessionStore() {
  return ctx.state();
}
```

